  "identifier": "medalign",
  "name": "MedAlign",
  "description": "Clinician-curated benchmark for evaluating LLM instruction-following on real clinical tasks. Contains 983 natural-language instructions authored by clinicians, paired with 275 de-identified longitudinal EHRs from Stanford Health Care. Instructions span a wide range of clinical reasoning tasks — summarisation, differential diagnosis, care plan generation, and follow-up ordering. Designed to assess whether LLMs can faithfully execute what a clinician actually asks, not just answer medical trivia. Dataset access requires a Stanford AIMI data use agreement; evaluation code is MIT. From the Shah Lab at Stanford Medicine.",
  "url": "https://github.com/som-shahlab/medalign",
